  "from": "the published article (PDF), read on the page text",
  "checked_against_source": true,
  "note": "Conductivities are divided by that of the matrix. All tables are for oblate spheroids of aspect ratio e = l3/l1 = 1/3, aligned with the axis x3. The low-conducting (Kapitza) interface has the parameter hc_tilde = l1 hc/k0 with the contrast k1/k0 = 1000; the highly conducting interface has hs_tilde = hs/(l1 k0) with k1/k0 = 0.1. The lattices are proportional: periods a1 = a2 and a3 = e a1; SP holds one spheroid per cell, BCP two (shift (a1, a2, a3)/2), FCP four (shifts (a1, 0, a3)/2, (a1, a2, 0)/2, (0, a2, a3)/2)."
 },
